diff --git a/docs/goose_spec.md b/docs/goose_spec.md
index b0ff6c2c..7c1d990d 100644
--- a/docs/goose_spec.md
+++ b/docs/goose_spec.md
@@ -2971,7 +2971,13 @@ cannot load SDL2 (libSDL2.so): libSDL2.so: cannot open shared object file: No su
 SDL2 (libSDL2.so) has no symbol SDL_Foo
 ```
 
-A library is never closed. A `main_thread_only` package (docs/packages.md)
+A library that exports `void goose_runtime_hooks(const gs_rt_hooks *)` is
+handed the runtime's hooks as it is opened (`goose.h` declares the struct):
+`abort_msg(msg, len, file, line)`, which ends the program exactly as
+`abort(msg)` does, or only the worker in a contained one (§11.2), and
+`at_end(fn)`, which has the runtime call `fn` when the program ends, by a
+return from `main` or by `exit`. A library never sees a hook it did not ask
+for. A library is never closed. A `main_thread_only` package (docs/packages.md)
 applies to its block's members as to its other externs. A variadic C
 function cannot be bound: the declaration has no way to say so, and
 calling one through a fixed-arity pointer is undefined. The generated C is
